VL  - 40
IS  - 4
SP  - 390
EP  - 394
DO  - 10.5937/jomb0-30616
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85115046076&doi=10.5937%2fjomb0-30616&partnerID=40&md5=5838450b4493eb9b2d5551227913e236
AB  - Background: Coronary artery diseases (CAD) are big health problem in both developed and developing countries. It is considered one of the main causes of death in the world. Dyslipidemia increases the risk of CAD incidences. It is aimed in this worktop study the impact of 3'APOBVNTRgene on CAD incidences. Methods: Eighty CAD patients and ninety-three healthy volunteers are enrolled in this study. Lipid parameters were estimated in both groups and PCR technique has been performed to analyze 3'APOB-VNTR gene polymorphism. Results: The genotypes 31/31, 31/37, 37/37 and 31/44 are more predominant in both groups. The frequency of 24/31 in CAD patients is (0.137) while it is completely absent in the control group. Our results show that there is an increase in the frequency of various genotypes (e.g., 17/31 and 21/34 genotypes) in the control group compared to theca patients group. Conclusions: 3'APOB-VNTR gene could probably be considered a risk factor for CAD incidences and may help to early diagnose them. © 2021 Sciendo. All rights reserved.
