TI  - Antihyperlipidemic and anti-hyperglycemic effects of Cymbopogon jwarancusa in high-fat high-sugar Diet model
PY  - 2018
T2  - Pakistan Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences
VL  - 31
IS  - 4
SP  - 1341
EP  - 1345
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85049650708&partnerID=40&md5=2befab0fd8f789214fa58d7b8dddb3df
AB  - Hyperlipidemia is the root cause for development of atherosclerosis, coronary heart Disease, Diabetes mellitus, obesity, hypertension and cerebral palsy. Cymbopogon jwarancusa is an aromatic grab (Rusha grab, khavi grab) belonging to family Poaceaea. C. jwarancusa ebential oil is famous for its use in perfumery, soaps cosmetics, detergents, medicine and pharmaceuticals. The anti-pyretic, anti-fungal, antibacterial, anti-oxidant and cytotoxic activities of C. jwarancusa have been reported in literature. In the present study different doses of C. jwarancusa extract have been investigated for anti-hyperlipidemic and anti-hyperglycemic activities in high-fat high sugar Diet model in rats. Hyperlipidemia and hyperglycemia were abebed by measuring body weight, serum lipid profile and fasting blood glucose levels. Administration of ethanol leaves extract of C. jwarancusa exhibited significant dose-dependent reduction in body weight, lipid parameters and blood sugar levels. Hence it may be concluded that C. jwarancusa AIDS in ameliorating hyperlipidemic, hyperglycemic condiitions and has potential to reduce the risk of cardiovascular problems. © 2018 Pakistan Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences. All rights reserved.
