AB  - The authors conducted a repeated examination of 150 patients suffering from ischemic heart disease with normolipidemia types IIa, IIb and IV hyperlipoproteinemia. The content of α-cholesterol in these patients tended to fluctuate, as did the content of other blood lipid fraction. Its fluctuations were most marked in types IIb an IV hyperlipoproteinemia. Comparison of the α-cholesterol content in patients with ischemic heart disease with the results of population tests confirmed the information on its lower level in patients. A still greater difference between patients and healthy individuals was revealed when the percentage of total cholesterol for which α-lipoproteins accounted and the value of the cholesterol atherogenic index were compared. Reduced concentration of α-cholesterol was encountered not only in hyperlipoproteinemia, but also in normolipidemia. The level of α-cholesterol had a negative correlative connection with the content of triglyericides in the blood.
