AB  - Cholesterol electrophoresis was made on 1184 male, healthy recruits and the atherogenic index was calculated (mean value 2.968 ± 0.802). The relationship between risk ratio and other risk factors of coronary artery disease was detected. Statisticaly high significance was found there with weight/height ratio (P<0.01), systolic and diastolic blood pressure (P<0.01), cholesterol values (P<0.01) and smoking status (P<0.05). The values of the index showed only a slight variation in different geographic areas within the country.
