AB  - The atherogenic index (Cholestrol/HDL-Cholest.) was calculated in a group of 921 healthy male recruits, 20 years old. The relationship between risk ratio and other risk factors of CHD was calculated. The most significant variable was found to be the weight/height ratio (P [ 0.001) followed by cholesterol level (P [ 0.001), Systolic blood pressure and diastolic blood pressure (P [ 0.001). The number of cigarettes smoked per day and the duration of the habit in years, were significant in correlation to the index (P [ 0.001). People living in industrial areas have shown a tendency for higher indexes in comparison with people coming from rural areas.
